Found a fix for `RENAME unsupported AS foo` which also fixes `RENAME multi_typed_field AS foo`. It required creating reference attributes from aliases even if the child expression is not fully resolved - which is exactly the case for `UnsupportedAttribute`, which is considered unresolved, but its type is resolved (to `UNSUPPORTED`).

@costin @astefan let's discuss whether we want to allow `RENAME` for unsupported/multi types before moving on with this fix.

(Side note: maybe the verification step could be simplified if we didn't consider `UnsupportedAttribute` as unresolvable. I suspect that the mechanism that allows passing through unsupported types could be simpler if we shifted the responsibility to the type resolution step only, i.e. don't fail a query just because we see an `UnsupportedAttribute`, but fail it when this is used in a place that requires something other than the `UNSUPPORTED` data type. It would prevent having to change `Alias.toAttribute` as well.)
